From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 349/349] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: limit
 the Wi-Fi PCIe link to Gen2

The Wi-Fi link on pcie0 trains Gen3 x2 at probe, and the controller
keeps the matching OPP: both Gen3 OPPs of pcie0_opp_table need the CX
rail at NOM, the Gen1 / Gen2 ones (x1 and x2) only LOW_SVS. The OPP and
interconnect votes are only refreshed at probe and resume, so the NOM
vote stays even after the link drops to Gen3 x1, and with the screen
off pcie0 is the only CX voter above zero on the tablet.

Gen2 x2 (8 Gbit/s, 4 Gbit/s at x1) is far above what the Wi-Fi link
carries here (112-133 Mbit/s TCP measured, 780 Mbit/s PHY rate). Stock
votes NOM for Gen3 as well but lets the hardware drop the vote in L1ss
(CESTA), which mainline does not have. Limit the link to Gen2.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 226050e78304..be9c4112fe6a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1665,6 +1665,13 @@ &mdss_dsi1_phy {
 };
 
 &pcie0 {
+	/*
+	 * The Wi-Fi link carries far less than Gen2 offers, and the Gen1 / Gen2
+	 * OPPs of pcie0 need only LOW_SVS on CX, while a Gen3 link holds CX at
+	 * NOM for as long as the link is up.
+	 */
+	max-link-speed = <2>;
+
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pcie0_default_state>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
-- 
